    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Marine Corps Air Station El Toro, once a bustling military hub, closed its gates in 1999 and later became a community space.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Forest%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Heritage Hill Historical Park preserves Orange County’s oldest buildings, including the 1863 Jose Serrano Adobe and El Toro’s first schoolhouse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Forest%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1888, the Santa Fe Railroad ran through the area, officially christening the settlement El Toro for the first time.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
